<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Ingestion Layer on AWS FCJ Capstone Report - Nguyen Ngoc Tuan Khanh</title><link>https://Oolongk.github.io/aws-project/en/2-workshop/2.3-clickstream/2-ingestion-layer/</link><description>Recent content in Ingestion Layer on AWS FCJ Capstone Report - Nguyen Ngoc Tuan Khanh</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Thu, 25 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://Oolongk.github.io/aws-project/en/2-workshop/2.3-clickstream/2-ingestion-layer/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Configure Kinesis Data Firehose</title><link>https://Oolongk.github.io/aws-project/en/2-workshop/2.3-clickstream/2-ingestion-layer/2.1-kinesis-firehose/</link><pubDate>Thu, 25 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://Oolongk.github.io/aws-project/en/2-workshop/2.3-clickstream/2-ingestion-layer/2.1-kinesis-firehose/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Kinesis Data Firehose acts as a streaming data reception station and performs format conversion (JSON to Parquet) directly on the data stream (on-the-fly).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4 id="step-by-step-deployment-guide"&gt;Step-by-step deployment guide&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
	&lt;thead&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;th style="text-align: left"&gt;Step&lt;/th&gt;
					&lt;th style="text-align: left"&gt;Action&lt;/th&gt;
					&lt;th style="text-align: left"&gt;Technical details&lt;/th&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
	&lt;/thead&gt;
	&lt;tbody&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;td style="text-align: left"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td style="text-align: left"&gt;Access AWS Console&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td style="text-align: left"&gt;Search for &lt;strong&gt;Kinesis&lt;/strong&gt; -&amp;gt; select &lt;strong&gt;Data Firehose&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;td style="text-align: left"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td style="text-align: left"&gt;Create Stream&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td style="text-align: left"&gt;Click &lt;strong&gt;Create delivery stream&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;td style="text-align: left"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td style="text-align: left"&gt;Configure Source&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td style="text-align: left"&gt;Select Source as &lt;strong&gt;Direct PUT&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;td style="text-align: left"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td style="text-align: left"&gt;Configure Destination&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td style="text-align: left"&gt;Select Destination as &lt;strong&gt;Amazon S3&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;td style="text-align: left"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td style="text-align: left"&gt;Enable compression feature&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td style="text-align: left"&gt;Find the &lt;strong&gt;Transform and convert records&lt;/strong&gt; section, select &lt;strong&gt;Enable&lt;/strong&gt; in the &lt;em&gt;Convert record format&lt;/em&gt; box.&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;td style="text-align: left"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;6&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td style="text-align: left"&gt;Select Format&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td style="text-align: left"&gt;Select Output format as &lt;strong&gt;Apache Parquet&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;td style="text-align: left"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;7&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td style="text-align: left"&gt;Point to AWS Glue Catalog&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td style="text-align: left"&gt;In the Schema configuration section, select the correct &lt;strong&gt;Database&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;clickstream_db&lt;/code&gt;) and &lt;strong&gt;Table&lt;/strong&gt; that the Crawler just generated in section 1.2.&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;td style="text-align: left"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;8&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td style="text-align: left"&gt;Configure target S3&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td style="text-align: left"&gt;In the Destination settings section, select your S3 Bucket and enter Prefix as &lt;code&gt;data/&lt;/code&gt;. Click Create.&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
	&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://Oolongk.github.io/aws-project/images/Clickstream/2-ingestion-layer/Firehose-1.png?featherlight=false&amp;amp;width=90pc" alt="Firehose configuration illustration"&gt;
&lt;img src="https://Oolongk.github.io/aws-project/images/Clickstream/2-ingestion-layer/Firehose-2.png?featherlight=false&amp;amp;width=90pc" alt="Firehose configuration illustration"&gt;
&lt;img src="https://Oolongk.github.io/aws-project/images/Clickstream/2-ingestion-layer/Firehose-2.5.png?featherlight=false&amp;amp;width=90pc" alt="Firehose configuration illustration"&gt;
&lt;img src="https://Oolongk.github.io/aws-project/images/Clickstream/2-ingestion-layer/Firehose-3.png?featherlight=false&amp;amp;width=90pc" alt="Firehose configuration illustration"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Data Simulator</title><link>https://Oolongk.github.io/aws-project/en/2-workshop/2.3-clickstream/2-ingestion-layer/2.2-data-simulator/</link><pubDate>Thu, 25 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://Oolongk.github.io/aws-project/en/2-workshop/2.3-clickstream/2-ingestion-layer/2.2-data-simulator/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;To provide the system with input data for AI training, I have built a Clickstream data simulator using Python. This simulator models the behavior of 3 user groups (Personas) with different weights, creating a dataset with realistic patterns.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4 id="step-0-create-dedicated-user-and-get-security-key-best-practice"&gt;Step 0: Create dedicated User and Get security key (Best Practice)&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To ensure absolute safety for the system (Principle of Least Privilege), we will NOT use the Admin account. Instead, I will create a dedicated anonymous IAM User that only has permission to push data to Kinesis Firehose.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>